; DeadTree — 5th Forest tree pick, added 2026-08-26 (content-variety pass, Task 5). A
; bare-branch silhouette, visually distinct from all 4 living-canopy picks (CommonTree1/2,
; PineTree, BirchTree) — scenery variety only, not implying anything about Forest's
; gameplay meaning (the tile still emits `forest` and harvests the same Wood regardless of
; which of the now-5 trees a given tile's stable hash lands on).
;
; Source: "DeadTree_3.fbx", Textured Stylized Trees (May 2020) by Quaternius, CC0 1.0
; Universal — License.txt at `source-content/assets/Textured Stylized Trees - May 2020.../
; License.txt` re-checked before import, per asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate (states
; CC0 1.0 Universal / Public Domain Dedication, same boilerplate as every other Quaternius
; pack in this repo). This is a NEW pack for this project (no prior entry existed) —
; recorded in the newly-authored
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_textured_stylized_trees.tres.
;
; SCALE: the source file bakes a 90-degree axis correction + scale=100 into its own child
; node (Blender Z-up -> FBX Y-up, same mechanism PineTree.tscn's header documents),
; measured post-correction global AABB height = 5.6187 units (footprint ~4.504 x 4.516 at
; that height) — scaled here by 0.392 to hit a ~2.2-tile canopy height, DELIBERATELY
; SHORTER than the other 4 trees' ~2.5-tile target: bare branches read visually taller/
; busier at a given height than a filled canopy, so this pass's proposal is to undershoot
; slightly rather than match height exactly. FIRST-PASS PROPOSAL, not a measured GDD
; number — FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF, both on the ~2.2 vs ~2.5 height judgment call itself and
; on whether a bare-branch tree reads correctly (not "broken"/"dead level") at the fixed
; ~45 camera pitch next to 4 living-canopy neighbors.
;
; SLAB IS 1.0x0.2x1.0 (matches every current-generation terrain slab, post the
; "SLAB WIDENED 0.94 -> 1.0" cross-tile seam fix PineTree.tscn's header documents).
;
; FLOOR TREATMENT MATCHES COMMONTREE1/COMMONTREE2/PINETREE/BIRCHTREE EXACTLY (same slab
; tint, same 3-patch moss/litter blotch treatment, same relative transforms) so a Forest
; tile's floor reads identically regardless of which of the now-5 trees it lands on.
;
; EVERYTHING NESTED UNDER ONE NODE NAMED "Slab" (required, not cosmetic): identical
; OcclusionFader exemption requirement as every sibling terrain scene — see
; CommonTree1.tscn's header for the full mechanism. The ground plane (renamed "Ground")
; and all 3 floor patches are children of a wrapper Node3D literally named "Slab".
;
; MATERIAL OVERRIDE ADDED (2026-08-26, human-reported bug: "some of the trees are just
; plain white"). Root cause: unlike BirchTree.fbx (Ultimate Nature Pack), this pack —
; "Textured Stylized Trees" — ships real bark/leaf textures rather than baked per-vertex
; color, but only the raw .fbx was copied into the project at import time; no texture ever
; accompanied it, so the FBX's "Bark" material had nothing to sample and Godot's importer
; fell back to a near-white default (measured albedo_color 0.9063/0.9063/0.9063,
; vertex_color_use_as_albedo=true reading empty per-vertex data). Fixed the same way
; Rabbit.tscn overrides its imported material (see that file for the precedent): the raw
; `Bark_Dead.png` texture (this pack's own dedicated dead-wood variant, `Textures/Color
; Variations/Bark_Dead.png` — chosen over the generic `Tree_Bark.jpg` PineTree2.tscn uses,
; since this is specifically the DEAD tree) was copied to
; `res://assets/terrain/dead_tree/Bark_Dead.png` and wired as a `surface_material_override`
; on the instanced FBX's "DeadTree_3" mesh node below, with `vertex_color_use_as_albedo`
; explicitly false so the texture is not multiplied against the (meaningless, near-white)
; per-vertex data. `[editable path="Model"]` is required for the override to apply to a
; node living inside an instanced sub-scene — omitting it is the mistake that would silently
; leave this override inert.
